  "relationship": "Independent native operation invokes the already attributed pinned default renderer. It preserves strict selection, pending-navigation prechecks, missing-target retries and original document ownership. No new upstream browser-command backend is used.",
  "contracts": [
    "Public Page and Locator default mode only; same-process frame locators retain original root and selected document checks. Public AI mode and remote-frame ARIA snapshots reject explicitly.",
    "Normalize options before trace owner lookup; application getters are read once. Getter traces retain action/result/source and filmstrip activity without DOM snapshot references.",
    "Requests and output each permit100000 UTF-16 units; excessive output rejects atomically. The output limit does not bound browser DOM/tree allocations or synchronous renderer CPU.",
    "One original operation owns inherited/explicit-zero deadlines, navigation prechecks, frame resolution and retry. Pinned default snapshot-map side effects are preserved.",
    "The private failure-context fallback is a separate operation and does not expand public AI support. This record is provenance, not a merged verification claim."
  ],
